      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The thing not mentioned by anyone, is that the difference between dynamic bones and the effects you mention, is that dynamic bones is a specific script that is individually implemented and properly named, where as those effects are shader based, and due to the nature of how shaders are scripted, it makes it very difficult to tell what it does visually without individually sifting through uploaded shaders with a human manually viewing what the end result is and flagging it appropriately.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
